{"name":"Backdrop","hex":"#a7a799","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"backdrop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A decorated cloth hung at the back of a stage.","An image that serves as a visual background."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To serve as a backdrop for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backdrop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Theater drapes and stage curtains","blocks":[{"text":"Theater drapes and stage curtains are large pieces of cloth that are designed to mask backstage areas of a theater from spectators. They are designed for a variety of specific purposes, moving in different ways and constructed from various fabrics. Many are made from black or other darkly colored, light-absorbing material. Theater drapes represent a portion of any production's soft goods, a category comprising any non-wardrobe, cloth-based element of the stage or scenery. Theater curtains are often pocketed at the bottom to hold weighty chain or to accept pipes to remove their fullness and stretch them tight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Stage_curtains.jpg/330px-Stage_curtains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theater_drapes_and_stage_curtains"},{"title":"Professional wrestling throws","blocks":[{"text":"Professional wrestling throws are the application of professional wrestling techniques that involve lifting the opponent up and throwing or slamming them down. They are sometimes also called \"power\" maneuvers, as they are meant to emphasize a wrestler's strength. Many of these moves are used as finishers by various wrestlers, who refer to them by several different names that reflect their gimmick. Moves are listed under general categories whenever possible."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Professional_wrestling_throws"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg/500px-PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg/500px-PANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Theatro Municipal do Rio de Janeiro, painting by Eliseu Visconti (1908).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APANO_DE_BOCA_DO_THEATRO_MUNICIPAL_DO_RIO_DE_JANEIRO_-_A_INFLU%C3%8ANCIA_DAS_ARTES_SOBRE_A_CIVILIZA%C3%87%C3%83O.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/86/AustrianPic.jpg/250px-AustrianPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/AustrianPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/86/AustrianPic.jpg/250px-AustrianPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Austrian curtain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustrianPic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Theater_Bielefeld_Inspizientenpult.jpg/500px-Theater_Bielefeld_Inspizientenpult.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Theater_Bielefeld_Inspizientenpult.jpg/1280px-Theater_Bielefeld_Inspizientenpult.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/